course: dictionary
lesson: 11873
title: Bounds: limits and leaps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so use the words around it to choose the right one. «The children must stay within the bounds of the playground.» Here bounds means the edges or limits of an area, the line you must not cross.
explain: «The dog bounds across the field.» Now bounds is an action word. The dog is doing something, so bounds means jumps or runs with big leaps. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something being done?
explain: Some phrases use bounds in a special way. «The storeroom is out of bounds.» means you are not allowed to go there. «Our reading has improved by leaps and bounds.» means it has improved very quickly. Learn these phrases as whole chunks.
fact: «Bounds» can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action word).
fact: As a noun, «bounds» means limits or borders: «within the bounds of the park».
fact: «Out of bounds» means a place you are not allowed to go, or outside the playing area in a game.
fact: «By leaps and bounds» means very quickly.
fact: As a verb, «bounds» means jumps or runs with big leaps: «The dog bounds across the field.»
exercise: «The children must stay within the bounds of the park.» What does bounds mean here? | *Limits or borders | A hidden treasure | Big leaps | Very quickly
exercise: «The dog bounds across the field.» What kind of word is bounds here? | An adjective, a describing word | *A verb, an action word | A noun, the name of a place | A question word
exercise: «The garden shed is out of bounds.» What does out of bounds mean? | *A place you are not allowed to go | A very fast race | A place full of flowers | A locked box that is empty
test: «Our team has improved by leaps and bounds this term.» What does by leaps and bounds mean? | Over a high wall | Very slowly | *Very quickly | In a loud voice
test: In maths, what is an upper bound? | The smallest value a number could have been | The answer to a sum | *The largest value a rounded number could have been | The number in the middle of a list
exam: «The lamb bounds over the wall.» Which word means the same as bounds here? | Limits | Walks | *Jumps | Sleeps
